<instruction name="VPMOVDW/VPMOVSDW/VPMOVUSDW">
 <copyright>Copyright (C) Intel Corporation. All Rights Reserved.</copyright>
 <shortdesc>Down Convert DWord to Word</shortdesc>
 <longdesc><para unique="1046274">
   <string>VPMOVDW down converts 32-bit integer elements in the source operand (the second operand) into packed words using truncation. VPMOVSDW converts signed 32-bit integers into packed signed words using signed saturation. VPMOVUSDW convert unsigned double-word values into unsigned word values using unsigned saturation. </string></para>
  <para unique="1046275">
   <string>The source operand is a ZMM/YMM/XMM register. The destination operand is a YMM/XMM/XMM register or a 256/128/64-bit memory location.</string></para>
  <para unique="1046276">
   <string>Down-converted word elements are written to the destination operand (the first operand) from the least-significant word. Word elements of the destination operand are updated according to the writemask. Bits (</string><sans><string>MAXVL-1</string></sans><string>:256/128/64) of the register destination are zeroed.</string></para>
  <para unique="1046277">
   <string>EVEX.vvvv is reserved and must be 1111b otherwise instructions will #UD.</string></para>
  </longdesc>
